The Wallet app in <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a> has a new "Create a Pass" option that's designed to let you add passes for tickets, memberships, and more using <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/visual-intelligence/">Visual Intelligence</a>. If you have a ticket for an event and there's not a digital version available in the Wallet app already, you can create one using the physical pass. <br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/06/ios-27-wallet-create-pass.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1051256" /><br/>
By default, the Wallet app uses &zwnj;Visual Intelligence&zwnj; to scan a pass and add it, but there's also a "Create Pass Manually" option. Pass templates include Standard, Membership, and Event. <br/>
<br/>
Each type includes relevant information like name, location, or admission type, along with a scannable code drawn from an included barcode or QR code that you take a photo of. There are 12 background colors to choose from, or seven custom backgrounds for categories like theater, music, sports, and movies. <br/>
<br/>
